{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790724615,"nonce":"sjd4w+h5HbCRXbSb9/6MjKSkGCA=","title":"Raw anonymous handles are mistaken for boxed Dynamic fields","message":"Issue11851 reads an anonymous object through an array returned by Reflect.field. Reflect.field(item, \"foo\") returns 1, but item.foo returns null. The dynamic field runtime treats any first-word value above 100 as a valid user type ID; a raw anonymous handle begins with an Arc pointer whose low bits often meet that condition.\n\nDynamic field dispatch should accept a user type ID only when it is registered, and otherwise use reflective lookup on the raw handle. The focused regression checks both field-read forms, Type.typeof, and a second field.\n\nReproducer: haxe-conformance/corpus/tests/unit/src/unit/issues/Issue11851.hx. Regression: haxe-conformance/regressions/ReflectArrayDynamicFields.hx.","files":null}]}